WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:08.897
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:14.787
Unit eight: Team Sports. Today you will contrast ideas using despite and although.

4
00:00:15.087 --> 00:00:17.774
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:22.024
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:23.780
Strategy.

7
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:27.828
Strategy means a plan to win or reach a goal.

8
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:30.532
Our coach has a clever strategy.

9
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:33.525
Your turn. Say: Strategy.

10
00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:37.554
Strategy.

11
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:39.271
Formation.

12
00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:43.026
Formation means how players stand on the field.

13
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:46.417
We played in a 4-4-2 formation.

14
00:00:47.017 --> 00:00:49.472
Your turn. Say: Formation.

15
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:53.288
Formation.

16
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.086
Substitute.

17
00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:59.081
Substitute means a player who replaces another.

18
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:02.043
The substitute scored in the last minute!

19
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.256
Your turn. Say: Substitute.

20
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.101
Substitute.

21
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:10.735
Captain.

22
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.877
Captain means the leader of a team.

23
00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:16.576
Our captain encouraged everyone.

24
00:01:17.183 --> 00:01:19.650
Your turn. Say: Captain.

25
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.373
Captain.

26
00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.025
Rivalry.

27
00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:29.595
Rivalry means strong competition between two teams.

28
00:01:30.183 --> 00:01:32.903
There is a big rivalry between the two schools.

29
00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:36.157
Your turn. Say: Rivalry.

30
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.059
Rivalry.

31
00:01:40.817 --> 00:01:42.062
Sportsmanship.

32
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.431
Sportsmanship means playing fairly and respecting others.

33
00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:49.539
Shaking hands shows good sportsmanship.

34
00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:53.081
Your turn. Say: Sportsmanship.

35
00:01:55.933 --> 00:01:57.306
Sportsmanship.

36
00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:58.993
Momentum.

37
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:03.214
Momentum means the power to keep winning or moving forward.

38
00:02:03.817 --> 00:02:05.805
After the goal, we had momentum.

39
00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:09.092
Your turn. Say: Momentum.

40
00:02:11.933 --> 00:02:12.969
Momentum.

41
00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:14.764
Underdog.

42
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.469
Underdog means the team people expect to lose.

43
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.025
We were the underdog, but we won.

44
00:02:21.617 --> 00:02:24.269
Your turn. Say: Underdog.

45
00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.146
Underdog.

46
00:02:28.883 --> 00:02:29.873
Defense.

47
00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:34.021
Defense means the players who stop the other team scoring.

48
00:02:34.617 --> 00:02:36.454
Our defense was very strong.

49
00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.575
Your turn. Say: Defense.

50
00:02:42.433 --> 00:02:43.342
Defense.

51
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:45.108
Offense.

52
00:02:46.117 --> 00:02:48.778
Offense means the players who try to score.

53
00:02:49.383 --> 00:02:50.977
Their offense was fast.

54
00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:54.120
Your turn. Say: Offense.

55
00:02:56.967 --> 00:02:57.933
Offense.

56
00:02:58.683 --> 00:02:59.603
Tactic.

57
00:03:00.617 --> 00:03:03.255
Tactic means a small plan used during a game.

58
00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.768
Passing short was a good tactic.

59
00:03:06.383 --> 00:03:08.490
Your turn. Say: Tactic.

60
00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:12.183
Tactic.

61
00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:13.789
Teamwork.

62
00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:17.201
Teamwork means working well together as a group.

63
00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:19.317
Teamwork won us the cup.

64
00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:22.256
Your turn. Say: Teamwork.

65
00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.031
Teamwork.

66
00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:30.612
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.717
Visal, I heard your team won the final!

68
00:03:34.817 --> 00:03:39.083
Yes! Despite being the underdog, we won two–one.

69
00:03:40.183 --> 00:03:41.335
How did you do it?

70
00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:46.737
Our captain had a smart strategy, and our defense was strong.

71
00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:48.967
Were you tired?

72
00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:55.000
Although we were very tired, we kept playing. Teamwork gave us momentum.

73
00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:57.808
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.265
Grammar focus: despite and although.

75
00:04:01.565 --> 00:04:02.787
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:03.483 --> 00:04:05.762
Despite being the underdog, we won.

77
00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:09.172
Although we were tired, we kept playing.

78
00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.280
Despite the rain, the match continued.

79
00:04:13.233 --> 00:04:17.720
After 'despite', use a noun or -ing. After 'although', use a full sentence.

80
00:04:18.483 --> 00:04:22.645
Be careful! Don't say: Despite we were tired, we won.

81
00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.018
Say: Although we were tired, we won.

82
00:04:27.318 --> 00:04:29.468
Use 'although' before a full sentence.

83
00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:33.140
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:33.933 --> 00:04:35.422
The Underdog Final.

85
00:04:35.722 --> 00:04:39.370
Our captain designed a smart strategy and formation for the final.

86
00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:43.643
The other school was stronger, and there was a big rivalry.

87
00:04:44.633 --> 00:04:47.271
Despite being the underdog, we did not give up.

88
00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:52.182
Although our best player was injured, a substitute scored a great goal.

89
00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:57.523
Our teamwork gave us momentum, and we showed good sportsmanship to the end.

90
00:04:58.633 --> 00:05:02.716
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.979
blank the rain, we played the match.

92
00:05:06.279 --> 00:05:09.898
A, Despite. B, Although. C, Because.

93
00:05:13.433 --> 00:05:15.828
The answer is A: Despite.

94
00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.960
The leader of a team is the blank.

95
00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:23.157
A, captain. B, substitute. C, underdog.

96
00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.874
The answer is A: captain.

97
00:05:30.017 --> 00:05:32.504
The team people expect to lose is the blank.

98
00:05:32.804 --> 00:05:36.794
A, underdog. B, defense. C, formation.

99
00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:42.484
The answer is A: underdog.

100
00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.840
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:47.683 --> 00:05:50.008
Why is teamwork important in sports?

102
00:05:58.817 --> 00:06:00.236
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:00.536 --> 00:06:09.806
Teamwork is important because no player can win alone. Although one player may be very good, the team wins when everyone works together.

104
00:06:10.106 --> 00:06:11.908
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:12.817 --> 00:06:16.781
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and despite and although.

106
00:06:17.081 --> 00:06:21.034
Today's value is teamwork. We can do more when we work together.

107
00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:24.137
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

108
00:06:24.437 --> 00:06:26.927
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

